# Git Workflow for Parallel Agents

- One implementation task = one branch and one worktree when possible.
- Agents never modify another agent's branch or worktree.
- Never force push, `reset --hard`, or rewrite shared history.
- No unrequested merge or rebase of shared branches (`main`, `develop`, or another agent's branch).
- Commits contain only task-related changes.
- Always report base SHA, final SHA, changed files, and `git status --short`.
- Reviewer does not silently fix implementation; report findings instead.
- Integrator integrates only reviewed work at approved SHAs.
- Conflicts are reported; do not guess through ambiguous merges.
- Do not push unless explicitly requested.
- Do not stash, reset, or discard another worktree's changes from a bootstrap or integration task.

Branch naming: `<type>/<domain>-<task>-v<version>` — e.g. `feat/control-tower-alert-ack-v0.1`, `fix/shipment-tenant-isolation-v0.2`, `chore/parallel-agent-system-v0.2`.

Worktrees: sibling paths only — `D:\Projects\freight-platform-<name>` or `D:\Projects\freight-platform-wt\<name>`. Never inside the main repo directory. See `docs/engineering/WORKTREE_PROCEDURE.md`.
